02:37.020 --> 02:42.010
<b>Episode 4: "Cherry Blossom Festival!"</b>

02:37.690 --> 02:41.530
to launch a surprise attack 
on the cherry blossom festival.

02:43.480 --> 02:46.020
I have no idea what you're talking about.

02:46.540 --> 02:49.980
You mean the Cherry Blossom Festival 
they hold every year?

02:49.980 --> 02:52.250
Is this some weird scheme again?

02:52.250 --> 02:55.400
Sounds pretty awesome! Who are we fighting?

02:55.720 --> 03:00.530
I think we should open a stall on the 
Saturday and Sunday of the festival.

03:00.530 --> 03:03.820
Then just say that 
from the start, you nerd.

03:03.820 --> 03:06.790
Does "detachment" 
mean we're gonna split up?

03:06.790 --> 03:11.210
Yeah. Closing the actual café for it 
would be putting the cart before the horse.

03:11.210 --> 03:14.920
There'll be a bunch of stalls with 
tasty food at the festival, right?!

03:14.920 --> 03:16.800
That sounds kinda fun!

03:16.800 --> 03:19.550
I gotta make a spring version 
of our uniform, then!

03:19.550 --> 03:22.510
We should come up with a spring menu, too.

03:22.510 --> 03:25.510
Yes! An updated menu!

03:26.000 --> 03:30.100
We can't rely on coffee alone 
for a surprise attack.

03:30.100 --> 03:33.680
You will immediately commence 
development of a new weapon.

03:34.720 --> 03:38.500
Could you stop talking like that? 
It's pissing me off.

03:40.990 --> 03:44.560
Let's see... 
Yeah, all of this should be enough.

03:44.560 --> 03:47.080
So what are you planning to make?

03:47.080 --> 03:48.370
Cookies.

03:48.960 --> 03:51.210
With cherry blossom liqueur in them.

03:52.280 --> 03:55.380
It'll be something people 
can eat while they walk.

03:55.710 --> 03:59.630
Doesn't liqueur... have alcohol in it?

03:59.630 --> 04:00.920
It'll be fine.

04:01.230 --> 04:03.240
The alcohol evaporates when it's cooked,

04:03.240 --> 04:04.680
so it's safe even for kids.

04:04.680 --> 04:08.040
That's not what I mean...

04:08.970 --> 04:11.130
I'll try making a test batch.

04:11.130 --> 04:12.830
R-Right...

04:13.810 --> 04:17.020
Got anything I can help out with?

04:21.710 --> 04:23.450
They smell so nice!

04:23.450 --> 04:27.000
The smell's fine, but the color...

04:27.000 --> 04:27.910
Hey!

04:29.000 --> 04:31.370
Is there anything I can help with?!

04:32.150 --> 04:34.210
No, there isn't. Quit yelling.

04:34.640 --> 04:38.380
What the heck? And I came home early, too!

04:38.380 --> 04:41.340
Are you saying I'm useless?!

04:41.340 --> 04:43.500
I never said anything like that.

04:43.500 --> 04:44.380
Hmph!

04:44.670 --> 04:46.410
Okay, uh...

04:46.410 --> 04:50.760
Oh, I'm planning to leave you in charge 
of the café during the festival.

04:51.150 --> 04:55.390
We'll want at least one person here 
who's capable of managing it.

04:55.710 --> 04:58.980
So I'll be counting on you, 
Management Genius!

05:00.850 --> 05:03.490
W-Well, I guess I have no choice!

05:03.820 --> 05:07.310
You can leave the café to me!

05:07.310 --> 05:08.890
The genius!

05:11.990 --> 05:15.040
I'll try a different liqueur this time.

05:15.040 --> 05:15.790
Okay.

05:16.980 --> 05:23.160
You know, it's pretty wild that 
I'm working here at the café with you.

05:24.000 --> 05:26.920
I never would've seen this coming back then.

05:26.920 --> 05:31.680
Oh, you mean when Grandma 
talked to you about me?

05:31.680 --> 05:35.730
I mean, when I went to Tokyo U, 
I had no plans to take over the business.

05:36.220 --> 05:39.400
But it helps that you're such a great cook.

05:39.400 --> 05:41.360
Did you study it somewhere?

05:41.660 --> 05:43.540
Not exactly...

05:43.890 --> 05:45.490
But... yeah, I guess...

05:46.120 --> 05:48.610
There was something that 
inspired me to try cooking.

05:49.360 --> 05:54.280
It was a restaurant I went to 
with my dad when I was little.

05:54.280 --> 05:57.000
Something there just smelled so amazing.

05:57.000 --> 06:00.330
Oh, like curry udon 
at a soba shop or something?

06:00.330 --> 06:04.380
No, it smelled even better.

06:05.060 --> 06:07.760
It was similar to the smell

06:08.400 --> 06:10.760
of your sweat when you've been working.

06:12.300 --> 06:14.330
Uh, you...

06:15.330 --> 06:16.710
Gotcha!

06:16.710 --> 06:17.630
Huh?!

06:17.630 --> 06:19.020
I was just kidding.

06:20.930 --> 06:24.860
<i>I don't know... Maybe I've gotten 
a little too friendly with her.</i>

06:29.400 --> 06:31.530
I can't hold back anymore!

06:31.530 --> 06:33.500
This is it! This is the smell!

06:33.500 --> 06:34.620
You <i>did</i> mean it?!

06:35.150 --> 06:37.700
They say the smell of a man's sweat

06:37.700 --> 06:42.080
has something in it that makes 
women excited, you know.

06:42.080 --> 06:45.160
So this is all your fault,

06:45.160 --> 06:46.810
Hayato-kun.

06:46.810 --> 06:47.840
Don't strip me!

06:48.330 --> 06:51.180
<i>Why is she like this?! 
She hasn't been drinking!</i>

06:53.080 --> 06:56.470
<i>Wait... is it just from 
the evaporated alcohol?!</i>

06:59.600 --> 07:01.850
I knew something seemed off.

07:02.240 --> 07:04.860
You were pretending to be 
working on new menu items,

07:05.160 --> 07:09.700
but you just wanted to get Kiku-chan 
drunk and fool around with her!

07:09.700 --> 07:11.820
N-No! She just—

07:11.820 --> 07:14.070
Come on, take it off already.

07:13.360 --> 07:14.070
Idi—

07:14.410 --> 07:17.320
You tricked me!

07:18.480 --> 07:21.940
I added more frills to make it look flowery.

07:23.170 --> 07:24.710
It's so cute!

07:24.710 --> 07:27.760
And the hair band 
uses cherry blossom flowers.

07:27.760 --> 07:30.090
This is awesome! It's like magic!

07:30.350 --> 07:33.590
You're gonna be an amazing 
designer, Ouka-san!

07:35.140 --> 07:38.810
What about you? Is there a career 
you're working toward?

07:38.810 --> 07:42.480
Me? I wanna be a hero of justice!

07:42.480 --> 07:45.060
Huh? Like a police officer?

07:45.060 --> 07:47.610
Nope! A hero of justice!

07:47.610 --> 07:52.320
I'll patrol the town, and if I see any 
bad guys, I'll punch their lights out!

07:53.920 --> 07:55.280
I see.

07:55.560 --> 07:56.670
Oh, yeah!

07:56.670 --> 08:00.660
Can the cherry blossom hair band 
be launched like a missile?

08:01.030 --> 08:02.740
A m-missile?

08:04.270 --> 08:06.380
Oh, Hayato-kun!

08:06.670 --> 08:10.510
Check it out! I made cherry blossom 
hair bands for a more springtime look...

08:10.510 --> 08:12.010
Let me see that!

08:12.580 --> 08:15.470
There you are!

08:15.470 --> 08:18.360
Stop it, Kiku-chan! Put your clothes on!

08:20.100 --> 08:22.980
Hayato-kun...

08:22.980 --> 08:24.980
Just cover up, would you?!

08:27.600 --> 08:31.160
Look! My flowers bloomed!

08:33.040 --> 08:34.260
Ami-chan...

08:34.680 --> 08:35.700
Yeah.

08:36.480 --> 08:39.960
Hayato-kun, you're like a magician!

08:39.960 --> 08:41.830
They're so pretty!

08:42.530 --> 08:45.480
There's a bad guy right next to us.

08:45.480 --> 08:46.960
Yep. There sure is.

08:48.810 --> 08:50.750
Punch his lights out!

08:50.750 --> 08:51.840
He legit flew.

08:52.360 --> 08:55.260
And? Did you come up with new menu items?

08:55.790 --> 08:56.840
No.

08:57.130 --> 08:59.430
We tried out a few, but nothing worked.

08:59.430 --> 09:00.970
I see.

09:01.680 --> 09:04.620
By the way, not that it matters, but...

09:04.620 --> 09:05.560
What?

09:05.950 --> 09:11.570
I have this recipe for springtime cookies 
that Grandma and I came up with.

09:11.880 --> 09:12.820
Want it?

09:13.940 --> 09:16.320
Why didn't you bring this up sooner?

09:16.670 --> 09:20.720
Because you kept going on about 
surprise attacks and new weapons.

09:20.720 --> 09:22.700
You were having so much fun 
sounding so cringy.

09:23.020 --> 09:24.480
I didn't have the heart.

09:24.480 --> 09:26.900
Please let me see it. I'll use it.

09:27.370 --> 09:28.460
Oh, really?

09:30.820 --> 09:32.670
We've been through a lot...

09:34.610 --> 09:37.180
But let's get this festival started!

09:37.180 --> 09:40.490
<i>Ono Shiragiku's Gentle Awakening!</i>

09:37.180 --> 09:43.100
<b>Ono Shiragiku's Gentle Awakening</b>

09:43.520 --> 09:44.650
Mph...

09:45.310 --> 09:46.140
Huh?!

09:46.800 --> 09:48.090
What is this?!

09:48.560 --> 09:51.690
Who played this prank on me?!

09:53.760 --> 09:55.600
Step right up!

09:55.600 --> 09:59.320
Try some coffee from Café Terrace Familia!

09:59.320 --> 10:03.540
We've got cherry blossom cookies 
as a spring special! They're delicious!

10:03.540 --> 10:06.910
What got into you? You're so fired up.

10:06.910 --> 10:10.440
Because we got this "full armor" 
powered-up version of our uniform.

10:10.440 --> 10:12.540
It's giving me extra strength!

10:12.860 --> 10:14.380
"Full armor"?

10:14.380 --> 10:15.310
Yeah!

10:15.310 --> 10:18.300
You Familia kids are just full of energy.

10:18.300 --> 10:20.600
Want some of my steamed tuna buns?

10:20.600 --> 10:22.220
And some sakura mochi?

10:23.560 --> 10:25.340
Thank you!

10:25.340 --> 10:27.640
Show a little restraint!

10:28.190 --> 10:31.900
Anyway, sorry we set up this stall 
alongside yours on such short notice.

10:31.900 --> 10:34.730
Nah, don't you worry about it.

10:34.730 --> 10:38.730
We all owe a lot to your grandma, after all.

10:39.150 --> 10:40.320
Really?

10:40.640 --> 10:42.750
We're rooting for you.

10:42.750 --> 10:45.200
If you need anything at all, 
just let us know.

10:45.200 --> 10:46.860
Thank you.

10:46.860 --> 10:48.470
Well, good luck!

10:48.920 --> 10:50.730
Hayacchi, coffee!

10:51.200 --> 10:52.460
Quit goofing off!

10:54.120 --> 10:55.590
That aside...

10:57.660 --> 10:59.910
Why did she even come here?

11:03.280 --> 11:04.540
Ouka-san!

11:04.970 --> 11:07.290
This steamed tuna bun is really good!

11:07.290 --> 11:08.650
Here! Here, here, here!

11:08.650 --> 11:11.800
Hey, stop! Her eyes are 
rolling back into her head!

11:11.800 --> 11:15.480
Aw, but the steamed 
tuna bun's gonna get cold.

11:16.860 --> 11:18.860
Oh, crap! Was I asleep?!

11:19.310 --> 11:22.350
Morning. You were sound asleep 
with quite a dumb look on your face.

11:22.350 --> 11:24.740
Wh-Why were you watching me sleep?!

11:25.890 --> 11:30.120
And Ami-chan, if you're so mad that 
you wanna kill me, just wake me up!

11:30.120 --> 11:33.510
Huh? If I wanted to kill you, 
I'd just hit you.

11:33.510 --> 11:35.000
That's scary.

11:36.050 --> 11:39.700
We're not that busy. 
You can go home if you want.

11:40.610 --> 11:42.330
I'll go wash my face!

11:44.720 --> 11:46.470
Jeez...

11:46.730 --> 11:49.460
Even if I'm sleep-deprived, 
how could I pass out like that?

11:50.950 --> 11:52.380
I gotta get it together!

11:55.240 --> 11:57.000
I-I'm sorry!

12:04.520 --> 12:07.370
Thank you for waiting. 
Here's your cherry blossom set.

12:08.020 --> 12:10.410
Yeah, no problems here.

12:10.410 --> 12:13.080
We've even got more customers 
coming over from the festival.

12:13.080 --> 12:14.620
<i>Glad to hear that.</i>

12:14.990 --> 12:16.490
I'll leave you to it, then.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.970
Thank you very much!

12:18.970 --> 12:21.210
Any word from Ouka?

12:21.210 --> 12:24.840
Nope. Did she fall asleep in the restroom?

12:25.680 --> 12:27.520
What is she doing?

12:27.520 --> 12:29.510
I said I don't want to!

12:29.510 --> 12:32.780
Aw, why not? It can wait until 
you're done with your work.

12:32.780 --> 12:35.730
We're having a drinking party 
after this is over.

12:35.730 --> 12:37.150
I won't be going!

12:37.600 --> 12:39.020
What the heck is she doing?

12:39.020 --> 12:40.040
Stop it!

12:40.040 --> 12:41.650
She's getting hit on.

12:42.660 --> 12:43.980
Hey!

12:43.980 --> 12:45.880
Don't just watch! Help me!

12:45.880 --> 12:48.150
Oh... Sorry about that.

12:49.470 --> 12:55.210
Sorry, but she works for me. 
Could you pick up girls somewhere else?

12:55.210 --> 12:57.550
Huh? And who are you?

12:57.550 --> 13:00.340
You look pretty young. 
How old are you, anyway?

13:00.730 --> 13:02.460
I'm eighteen.

13:02.460 --> 13:06.360
Listen, you're blocking customers 
from getting to our stall.

13:06.360 --> 13:07.840
Could you please move?

13:07.840 --> 13:09.630
We're customers, too!

13:09.630 --> 13:12.100
We'll buy your damn coffee or whatever it is!

13:12.100 --> 13:14.360
Can I hit them so they go away?

13:14.360 --> 13:15.730
Don't.

13:15.730 --> 13:18.240
Hey, that one's a cutie, too!

13:18.240 --> 13:20.610
Sure, go ahead and hit us.

13:20.970 --> 13:23.610
Hey! No causing trouble 
in front of our stalls!

13:23.990 --> 13:26.360
If you've got a problem, 
how 'bout you take it up with me?

13:26.360 --> 13:28.560
Oh, you wanna go?

13:28.560 --> 13:30.760
Keep your voice down!

13:31.630 --> 13:34.790
If you're gonna interfere with 
our business, we'll call the police.

13:34.790 --> 13:36.560
Yeah! Get outta here!

13:36.560 --> 13:40.500
If you make trouble in front of 
Kasukabe-san's business, you'll regret it!

13:42.790 --> 13:46.550
Let's go. Their coffee's probably 
too gross to drink anyway.

13:46.550 --> 13:47.690
Move it!

13:49.270 --> 13:51.740
All of these stalls look like shit!

13:52.640 --> 13:56.940
Don't you worry. We'll run off 
punks like them anytime.

13:57.230 --> 14:00.650
You just do your best to keep 
your grandma's business going.

14:02.500 --> 14:04.890
I will. Thank you.

14:06.100 --> 14:07.880
That really happened?

14:07.880 --> 14:11.240
Ami-chan, next time you see 
those guys, just waste 'em!

14:11.240 --> 14:12.320
Got it!

14:12.320 --> 14:14.450
No, don't. It won't help anyone.

14:14.860 --> 14:18.210
Anyway, business is going great now.

14:18.510 --> 14:22.090
Let's keep this momentum 
going tomorrow, everyone!

14:22.090 --> 14:23.050
Yep!

14:23.050 --> 14:24.710
You got it!

14:23.050 --> 14:24.710
We'll do our best!

14:26.570 --> 14:29.680
Well, let's get this day started.

14:29.680 --> 14:32.570
I hope we'll draw a good crowd again today.

14:33.250 --> 14:34.750
For real?

14:34.750 --> 14:37.750
What's going on? 
They're in front of our stall.

14:42.900 --> 14:44.750
Wh-What is all this?

14:44.750 --> 14:46.700
I bet it was those guys from yesterday.

14:46.700 --> 14:48.030
This is awful...

14:48.030 --> 14:50.880
I'm pretty sure that was Fuwa-san's grandson.

14:50.880 --> 14:52.300
For cryin' out loud...

14:52.300 --> 14:56.040
That boy uses his grandpa's influence 
to do whatever he wants.

14:57.820 --> 14:59.630
<i>He's that guy's...</i>

14:59.630 --> 15:01.630
H-Hey, don't worry about it!

15:01.630 --> 15:03.880
Let's get this cleaned up.

15:04.190 --> 15:07.050
He's right. Let's open up your stall.

15:07.440 --> 15:10.330
No, we'll be withdrawing it.

15:11.000 --> 15:11.800
But...

15:12.120 --> 15:17.500
If this goes on, it might cause 
trouble for all of you again.

15:19.670 --> 15:22.300
Ugh, my hands still reek.

15:22.810 --> 15:25.220
Some of that garbage was kitchen waste.

15:29.570 --> 15:30.700
I'm sorry.

15:31.230 --> 15:33.790
I brought those guys to our stall.

15:33.790 --> 15:34.950
Ouka-san...

15:35.760 --> 15:37.960
I even fell asleep on the job.

15:38.480 --> 15:41.460
I've done nothing but get 
in the way. I'm useless.

15:42.690 --> 15:45.860
It's fine. Falling asleep won't kill anyone.

15:47.180 --> 15:52.090
You stayed up all night 
finishing those uniforms.

15:52.090 --> 15:55.970
B-But... Because of me...

15:55.970 --> 15:58.760
we had to close down the stall.

15:59.690 --> 16:03.350
All I said was that we'd withdraw our stall.

16:04.180 --> 16:06.480
I never said we were giving up.

16:09.000 --> 16:12.290
Ouka, I need your help.

16:12.290 --> 16:13.410
My help?

16:13.880 --> 16:16.900
Like hell I'm gonna just 
take a loss and live with it.

16:18.080 --> 16:22.060
Café Terrace Familia's 
counterattack starts now.

16:23.750 --> 16:26.040
They came back to the café in a hurry.

16:26.040 --> 16:27.690
Where'd they go now?

16:27.690 --> 16:31.510
They said they had something to do 
in the storage shed out back.

16:32.150 --> 16:33.430
Come on, now.

16:33.740 --> 16:37.130
Let Master handle our branch operations.

16:38.720 --> 16:42.230
We need to focus our attention 
on the main café!

16:44.180 --> 16:47.190
Yeah! I think it looks really cute now!

16:47.190 --> 16:49.610
Yeah. Looks good.

16:49.610 --> 16:51.440
That's an aspiring designer for you.

16:52.480 --> 16:54.450
I didn't know we had something 
like this, though!

16:55.110 --> 16:59.950
Grandma used it before she opened this café.

17:01.060 --> 17:04.730
It's called Café Terrace Familia: Type 0!

17:03.500 --> 17:07.670
<b>Café Terrace Familia Type 0</b>

17:04.730 --> 17:06.640
Ooh, that's so cool!

17:06.640 --> 17:08.590
It's just a food cart.

17:09.100 --> 17:12.960
I'm glad we got permission to run 
a mobile business just in case.

17:13.240 --> 17:16.400
Ami, load up the cart and get it moving!

17:16.400 --> 17:17.220
Yes, sir!

17:17.580 --> 17:21.470
Ouka, get Riho to post 
about this on our social media.

17:22.240 --> 17:25.310
Have her say, "Café Terrace Familia 
Type 0 is ready to counterattack.

17:26.100 --> 17:29.610
All those who need assistance, 
reply to this post!"

17:30.120 --> 17:33.920
By which you mean, 
"We're selling coffee via food cart,

17:33.920 --> 17:37.320
so if you're in the area, 
please come see us."

17:37.320 --> 17:38.570
Yes!

17:38.570 --> 17:43.200
Ami, I'm giving you one other 
special mission that only you can do.

17:43.200 --> 17:43.940
Yes, sir!

17:45.600 --> 17:47.240
Thank you for waiting.

17:48.080 --> 17:50.600
Two coffees and an order of cookies, please.

17:50.600 --> 17:51.800
Sure!

17:51.800 --> 17:53.460
Two caffè lattes, please.

17:53.710 --> 17:55.130
Coming up!

17:55.130 --> 17:58.220
Look at all these people. 
Why are there so many?

17:58.220 --> 17:59.970
It was all Riho.

17:59.970 --> 18:02.850
<b></b>#CherryBlossomFestival #Cafe #Coffee
How about a coffee to enjoy while you
observe the blossoms? We're running a
food cart in the area, so please stop by!

17:59.970 --> 18:02.850
She's been replying to everyone 
she finds on social media

18:02.850 --> 18:04.670
who's out to see the cherry blossoms.

18:04.670 --> 18:05.740
There.

18:05.740 --> 18:07.080
Riho-chan!

18:07.080 --> 18:08.230
Coming!

18:08.600 --> 18:12.110
But with this many customers, 
our supplies won't last.

18:12.110 --> 18:15.740
Don't worry about that. 
I've secured a supply line.

18:16.040 --> 18:17.070
Supply line?

18:17.070 --> 18:19.080
I'm back!

18:22.120 --> 18:26.540
I brought cookies, water, 
and beans from the café!

18:27.780 --> 18:30.880
Ami-chan, did you actually 
run there and back?!

18:30.880 --> 18:32.330
Well, yeah!

18:33.160 --> 18:35.920
Sorry for asking you to do this.

18:36.190 --> 18:38.840
My strength is the one thing 
I've got going for me!

18:38.840 --> 18:41.640
If you run low on anything, 
I'll go as many times as it takes!

18:42.880 --> 18:44.570
There it is!

18:45.600 --> 18:50.440
Wow, the waitresses' uniforms 
are just as cute as the stall!

18:50.440 --> 18:51.740
They really are!

18:51.740 --> 18:53.160
Th-Thank—

18:53.160 --> 18:54.840
She designed them.

18:55.770 --> 18:57.080
Amazing, aren't they?

18:57.750 --> 18:59.570
I-It's not...

18:59.880 --> 19:03.700
She's working for us part-time 
in hopes of being a designer one day.

19:03.700 --> 19:08.570
Really? Then we'll take two coffees 
as a show of our support.

19:09.520 --> 19:11.500
Well, don't just stand there, Ouka.

19:11.500 --> 19:13.310
Oh... I'm sorry!

19:13.310 --> 19:14.940
And you unload the stuff, Ami.

19:14.940 --> 19:16.250
Yes, sir!

19:18.950 --> 19:20.510
If that many people were going to come,

19:20.960 --> 19:23.750
we should've used the cart 
from the beginning.

19:24.160 --> 19:25.510
Nope.

19:25.510 --> 19:29.480
This strategy has one fatal flaw.

19:30.190 --> 19:32.400
I don't have the physical strength for this!

19:32.880 --> 19:36.520
Now, that's just pathetic. 
Get it together, Master!

19:36.520 --> 19:39.710
Oh! Wanna start jogging with me tomorrow?

19:39.710 --> 19:41.150
I do not!

19:41.810 --> 19:44.410
Anyway, stay alert.

19:44.700 --> 19:45.440
Huh?

19:45.440 --> 19:48.470
Enemy planes are known 
to fly along this route.

19:49.200 --> 19:52.580
Hey, you're the crew from yesterday.

19:53.650 --> 19:55.020
Oh, come on.

19:55.020 --> 19:59.670
Your stall got trashed to hell, 
and you still haven't learned?

19:59.670 --> 20:04.180
Who gave you permission to run 
your shop in front of my house?

20:04.180 --> 20:08.520
Bad luck for you, running into us 
in a deserted place like this.

20:08.520 --> 20:11.680
We'll trash that scuzzy cart of yours, too.

20:12.140 --> 20:14.330
So it <i>was</i> you guys.

20:14.330 --> 20:17.070
Destroying other people's 
property is a crime.

20:17.070 --> 20:19.450
Well, you piss me off...

20:19.450 --> 20:20.820
so I don't care!

20:23.290 --> 20:24.820
H-Hayato-kun!

20:25.300 --> 20:28.820
My grandpa has connections with the police.

20:30.090 --> 20:32.760
In the event of imminent 
and unlawful infringement,

20:32.760 --> 20:35.870
there's no punishment for actions taken 
to protect oneself or others

20:35.870 --> 20:38.210
when no other options are available.

20:38.510 --> 20:41.090
Huh? What're you talking about?

20:41.680 --> 20:44.400
Section 1, Article 36 of the penal code:

20:44.400 --> 20:46.470
the definition of legitimate self-defense.

20:55.350 --> 20:56.960
Wh-What the hell?!

20:56.960 --> 20:58.730
My special mission.

20:59.070 --> 21:01.880
Even if bad guys show up, 
just observe quietly.

21:01.880 --> 21:05.200
But as soon as I see 
Hayacchi getting attacked...

21:05.520 --> 21:09.330
Immediate initiation of 
legitimate self-defense!

21:13.300 --> 21:15.850
Pulverize the assailant with one strike!

21:17.070 --> 21:19.540
Th-That was amazing, Ami-chan!

21:22.550 --> 21:23.700
Huh?

21:24.500 --> 21:28.300
Crap! All that running back and forth 
sapped her strength!

21:34.310 --> 21:38.710
Die, you stupid bitch!

21:39.470 --> 21:41.940
Missiles, launch!

21:47.860 --> 21:51.860
Shoryuken!

21:56.520 --> 22:00.040
What the heck was that? 
The thing on your head...

22:00.040 --> 22:03.840
Oh, they're missiles! She made them for me!

22:04.200 --> 22:07.720
I never thought you'd 
actually use them...

22:07.720 --> 22:10.440
Wh-What is with this chick?

22:10.440 --> 22:12.430
She's strong as hell!

22:13.650 --> 22:16.560
Be glad it was Ami you were up against.

22:17.620 --> 22:19.200
The strongest one at our café

22:19.200 --> 22:21.060
is the legendary female gang leader...

22:21.440 --> 22:23.540
Mad Dog Ouka-san!

22:24.160 --> 22:25.280
What?!

22:25.320 --> 22:26.990
<b>Mad Dog</b>

22:25.860 --> 22:28.640
If she'd been the first one to get pissed,

22:28.640 --> 22:32.300
she would've snapped all your necks 
and dumped you in the lake.

22:32.300 --> 22:34.410
Who are you calling a mad dog?!

22:37.460 --> 22:39.710
We're sorry!

22:40.190 --> 22:42.400
Well, that should do it.

22:42.400 --> 22:45.340
I doubt they'll ever mess with us again.

22:45.780 --> 22:47.590
What makes you think that?

22:47.900 --> 22:50.800
The best way to ensure someone 
never picks a fight with you again

22:50.800 --> 22:54.350
is to show them you have 
the overwhelming edge in strength.

22:54.350 --> 22:58.100
<b>newrecording1.wav</b>

22:54.670 --> 22:58.100
And I did record our conversation, 
just in case.

22:56.290 --> 22:59.260
<i>Hey, you're the crew from yesterday.</i>

22:59.260 --> 23:00.270
<i>Oh, come—</i>

23:00.880 --> 23:04.540
I-If you were doing that, 
why'd you let him hit you?!

23:04.540 --> 23:06.460
What if you'd been seriously hurt?

23:05.670 --> 23:07.110
Tatsumaki Senpukyaku!

23:07.590 --> 23:11.110
If I'd just stood there quietly, 
they would've wrecked the cart.

23:11.500 --> 23:12.740
Huh?

23:13.880 --> 23:16.600
And you went to all that trouble 
to make it look nice.

23:16.600 --> 23:18.970
I wasn't gonna let them lay a finger on it.

23:26.400 --> 23:30.870
Then you should've fought them yourself 
instead of making Ami-chan do it!

23:31.490 --> 23:34.730
Oh, yeah. That's our big, 
scary Mad Dog Ouka-san.

23:34.730 --> 23:36.970
Again, who are you calling a mad dog?!

23:36.970 --> 23:40.570
Come on, let's go home already! I'm hungry!

23:41.980 --> 23:56.990
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

23:41.980 --> 23:56.990
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

23:42.500 --> 23:44.120
Honkity-honk! Honkity-honk!

23:44.120 --> 23:47.320
That's the legendary female 
gang leader, Mad Dog Ouka-san!

23:47.320 --> 23:49.780
All of you, stick with me.

23:49.780 --> 23:50.570
Yes'm!

23:50.570 --> 23:53.130
That's how Familia, 
the legendary ladies who would later

23:53.130 --> 23:54.910
conquer the entire nation, were born.

23:54.910 --> 23:56.680
Honkity-honk! Honkity-honk!
